**How to implement.** `EpsAxisEvaluated` and the custom equality are deleted, so every axis is data and `EpsAxisDispersion` takes F#'s structural equality (001 §B; .spec-md §0.1, first row). After steps 2, 5, 7 and 8, nothing produces the case. (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`: delete `EpsAxisEvaluated` (`:369`), its `complexIndex` arm, `[<CustomEquality; NoComparison>]` (`:365`) and the `Equals` / `GetHashCode` overrides (`:380-394`). The doc comment above `RealNkFormulas` (`:346-356`) moves above `EpsAxisDispersion` and lists its data cases: term data (`RealNK`, `ComplexEps`), the tabulated table, the four oscillator laws and the published laws. (2) The dead arms are deleted: `parameters`' `SumOfTerms` arm (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:433-435`), `facetKey` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs:95`) and `isEditable` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:867`). `isEditable`'s predicate then reads: an axis is editable exactly when it is `RealNK` or `ComplexEps` term data. Every doc comment that names the evaluated closure is rewritten: `DispersionModels.fs`' module doc (`:10-23`) and the docs of `toEpsAxis`, `toEpsValue` and `toOpticalProperties`; `LibraryFacets.fs:82-90` and `:99-104`; and `MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:854-863`. (3) The two out-of-band fixtures build a flat data axis where they built `EpsAxisEvaluated (fun _ -> …)`: `OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs:37-38` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs:52-53`. The axis is a constant `RealNK` with n = 1.5 and k = 0, because the diagnostic reads only the segment intervals. (4) `Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs` gains `Equal axis data of every case is equal and hashes equal, and a changed value breaks equality`. For `RealNK`, `ComplexEps`, `TabulatedNK`, the four law cases and `PublishedLawAxis`, two separately built equal values MUST be equal with equal hashes, and changing one coefficient, sample or law MUST make them unequal. (5) Afterwards no file under `Berreman/` names `EpsAxisEvaluated`, in code or in a comment. S1.2's invariant `s02-no-eps-axis-evaluated` greps for it from S1.2's first step on.

**Acceptance.** After the case is deleted, unit-tests (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests) MUST pass with the structural-equality fact; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-tests (OutOfBandBadgeTests, MaterialEditorWindowTests, MaterialsWindowTests) and ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.
